1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,879
Cent #1328.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:05,160
In the words of the art historian Rosalind

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:08,980
Krauss, in her 1977 essay "Notes on the Index":

4
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,039
"Almost everyone is agreed about '70s art.

5
00:00:12,439 --> 00:00:15,359
It is diversified, split, factionalized."

6
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:17,480
Beneath that variety,

7
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:20,460
she saw one shared logic: the index.

8
00:00:21,339 --> 00:00:23,239
In that art, the record of a physical

9
00:00:23,359 --> 00:00:25,760
presence replaces the conventions of style.

10
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:28,440
Indexes are signs with a physical

11
00:00:28,539 --> 00:00:29,800
link to what they stand for,

12
00:00:30,079 --> 00:00:32,759
like footprints, cast shadows, or photographs.

13
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:35,859
In her words: "They are the marks or traces

14
00:00:35,899 --> 00:00:38,859
of a particular cause, and that cause is the thing

15
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:41,500
to which they refer, the object they signify."

16
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:44,299
The marks on a Cent are of this

17
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:46,420
kind: traces of real events,

18
00:00:46,759 --> 00:00:50,219
of wear, of damage, of the slow work of air.

19
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,420
Cent #1328 was struck in 1979,

20
00:00:54,659 --> 00:00:56,159
the year Rutherford Chang was born,

21
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:57,359
with no mint mark,

22
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,539
generally indicating the Philadelphia mint.

23
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,159
Its first trait is a fingerprint.

24
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,000
The ridges run across Lincoln's

25
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,819
neck and into the field beside him.

26
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:08,640
The Traits Atlas sets a strict bar:

27
00:01:09,099 --> 00:01:10,980
"if one hesitates to see a fingerprint,

28
00:01:11,239 --> 00:01:12,439
it isn't a Fingerprint."

29
00:01:13,439 --> 00:01:15,700
224 Cents carry it.

30
00:01:17,819 --> 00:01:20,200
Its second trait is White Drips and Streaks:

31
00:01:20,599 --> 00:01:21,840
pale runs of residue,

32
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,599
like this one falling from the rim.

33
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:26,400
Of the 82 Cents with this trait,

34
00:01:26,700 --> 00:01:29,400
79 are also Desert, a pale toning.

35
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:32,739
This is one of three that are not:

36
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:35,280
here the white runs over bright copper.

37
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:38,140
Only three Cents carry both traits,

38
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,280
and this is the only one with no other.

39
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:43,000
Compare Cent #1605,

40
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:45,780
also from 1979 and close to mint state.

41
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,140
An index points back to its cause.

42
00:01:49,879 --> 00:01:51,420
Here, the cause is a finger,

43
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:53,280
and whose, no one knows.

44
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,079
Someone has dreamed of finding out.

45
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:58,579
In the words of collector m4rtr3d:

46
00:01:59,859 --> 00:02:02,000
"I dream someday to be able to match one

47
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,000
of the fingerprints found on a few Cents,

48
00:02:04,219 --> 00:02:06,379
with the real person owning that fingerprint,

49
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,120
it would be a kind of cosmic

50
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:09,580
reconciliation of sorts."

51
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:13,979
Cent #1328, a great Cent.
